course: dictionary
lesson: 13422
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the clues around a word show you which one the writer means. «The hives were humming in the orchard.» Humming is a bee sound, so hives here means homes for bees.
explain: «Mia got red hives after eating strawberries.» Red bumps on the skin are the clue. Here hives means itchy red or pink bumps on the skin, not bee homes. Ask yourself which meaning fits the words around it.
explain: Hives is also the plural of hive: one hive, two or more hives. If hives come with swelling of the lips or face, or trouble breathing, it is an emergency, and an adult must call for help straight away.
fact: Hives can mean itchy red or pink bumps or patches on the skin.
fact: Skin hives can be caused by an allergy to food, medicine, insect stings or plants.
fact: A hive is a home for bees, and hives is the plural: many bee homes.
fact: Beekeepers keep bees in hives to collect honey.
fact: If hives come with swelling of the lips or face, or trouble breathing, get an adult to call for help at once.
exercise: «Sam broke out in hives after the bee sting.» What are hives in this sentence? | A kind of flower | A jar of honey | *Itchy red or pink bumps on the skin | A home for bees
exercise: «The beekeeper checked the hives in the garden.» What does hives mean here? | Itchy bumps on the skin | *Homes for bees | Bags of flour | Garden tools
exercise: Two beehives in the garden are two what? | hiver | hivings | *hives
test: What does hives mean in «Mum put cream on the hives on Ben's arm»? | Homes for bees | *Itchy red bumps on the skin | Boxes of honey | Garden sheds
test: Which sentence uses hives to mean bee homes? | «Her hives were red and itchy after the walk.» | *«The hives hummed all summer in the orchard.» | «The hives on his leg were getting bigger.»
exam: Lily broke out in hives, her lips swelled, and she had trouble breathing. What should happen? | Wait until the spots fade | *Get an adult to call for help straight away | Give her a drink and let her rest | Take her outside for some fresh air
